## Anti-Patterns / Failure Modes

- Reviewing style/formatting when fault-posture or intent issues are present
  (wrong priority order — always surface P1/P2 findings before nitpicks).
- Asserting architecture fit from inference without flagging it as inferred.
- Collapsing `NO_TEST_EXISTS` and `HIL_REQUIRED` into one "missing test"
  bucket — loses actionable signal.
- Approving on "looks right" pattern-matching without tracing against stated
  intent.
- Treating absence of a crash/error in a quick read as evidence of correct
  fault recovery — recovery must be traced, not assumed.
- **The Context Story reading like a mission statement or marketing copy**
  ("this change improves system reliability and performance") instead of a
  concrete causal chain a stranger could actually follow. If it could apply
  to almost any change, it's too vague.
- **The Blind Spot Story restating a Pass 2 table finding in prose** instead
  of surfacing a genuine gap in the approach. If it reads like "Path X is
  missing detection, severity blocking" with different words, it isn't a
  blind spot story — it's a table row wearing a costume.
- **Padding either story to hit a length target**, or inventing a blind spot
  to avoid an empty section — an honest "no blind spot rises above bug-level
  in this change" is a valid and useful output.
- **Writing either story in the same register as the technical findings**
  (dense, acronym-heavy) — if a freshman engineering generalist would need
  to ask what half the sentence means, it hasn't met the bar.

## Quality Gate

Before this skill moves `draft → validated`:
- [ ] At least 2 worked examples from real review sessions, ideally from
      different systems (to prove the Project Context argument pattern
      actually generalizes), including one catch a naive/generic review
      would have missed.
- [ ] Resolution order (Project Context > repo docs > skill defaults >
      inference) exercised and confirmed on at least one real conflict case.
- [ ] Severity defaults reviewed and confirmed by owner.
- [ ] At least one worked example includes a Context Story and Blind Spot
      Story reviewed by the owner for tone (would this actually land with a
      generalist reader?) and substance (is the blind spot a real gap in the
      approach, not a restated finding?).
- [ ] Owner sign-off (status change requires explicit user approval per
      project governance — no auto-publish).

